1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,225
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 8.

2
00:00:04,845 --> 00:00:08,465
What four values of x does the second pair of nested loops print?

3
00:00:10,165 --> 00:00:12,842
x starts at one, and the elements are read in row

4
00:00:12,842 --> 00:00:16,124
order: minus four, zero, minus three, two.

5
00:00:16,745 --> 00:00:19,865
Minus four is below minus one times ten to the minus

6
00:00:19,865 --> 00:00:23,646
seven, so x plus equals minus four: minus three.

7
00:00:24,265 --> 00:00:26,862
Zero is neither below minus ten to the minus

8
00:00:26,862 --> 00:00:30,167
seven, nor above plus ten to the minus seven.

9
00:00:30,167 --> 00:00:35,891
So the else runs: x minus equals one hundred, which gives minus one hundred three.

10
00:00:36,511 --> 00:00:41,498
Minus three: x plus equals minus three, giving minus one hundred six.

11
00:00:41,498 --> 00:00:46,841
Then two is positive: x minus equals ten, giving minus one hundred sixteen.

12
00:00:48,441 --> 00:00:53,899
This is an if, else if, else ladder: exactly one branch runs for each element.

13
00:00:53,899 --> 00:00:57,332
The tolerances, plus or minus ten to the minus seven,

14
00:00:57,332 --> 00:01:00,539
are a safe way to decide whether a double is zero.

15
00:01:02,139 --> 00:01:05,678
So x is printed as minus three, minus one hundred three,

16
00:01:05,678 --> 00:01:09,216
minus one hundred six, and minus one hundred sixteen.

17
00:01:10,037 --> 00:01:12,546
Sending zero into the positive branch.

18
00:01:12,546 --> 00:01:17,173
Zero is not greater than ten to the minus seven, so it goes to the else.

19
00:01:17,893 --> 00:01:20,743
Exam tip: for each element, test the conditions

20
00:01:20,743 --> 00:01:23,437
top to bottom and stop at the first true one.

21
00:01:23,437 --> 00:01:25,820
Write the branch you took in the table.
